        "math_academy_id": "q-18309",
        "problem": "Let $A(5,-1,1)$ and $B(0,-2,3).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|.$",
        "worked_solution": "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=5i-j+k, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=-2j+3k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\  & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2j+3k)-(5i-j+k) \\\\  & =-5i-j+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
